<VI _name="lvai_add_class_method.vi" description="Make an AIXML-generated VI a MEMBER of a LabVIEW class\2C retype its class-typed connector pane terminals\2C and set the ones that should dispatch to DYNAMIC DISPATCH - all in ONE run.\0A\0AWHY ONE RUN. Measured 2026-09-02 over a four-method DAQmx class\3A driving the retype\2C the membership and the wire rules as separate helpers cost about 105 s of wall clock for 3.3 s inside LabVIEW\2C and a misdiagnosis on top of that cost 70 s more. The sequence never varies\2C which is the signature of a step that should be a tool.\0A\0AORDER MATTERS AND IS NOT THE OBVIOUS ONE. Replace the terminals\2C then AddItemFromMemory\2C then SetWireRule\2C then the VI's own Save.Instrument\2C then the class Save. Saving the VI before it is a member writes it with no owning-library link\2C LabVIEW then sees library and VI disagree\2C marks the LIBRARY broken\2C and the library blocks EVERY VI it owns - which reads as Error 1003 on unrelated members.\0A\0ASAVE.INSTRUMENT ALONE DOES NOT PERSIST A REPLACE ON A CLASS MEMBER. The owning class must be saved in the SAME run\3B measured 2026-09-02\2C a run that saved only the VI reported success and left the on-disk file unretyped\2C which then read back as a healthy VI through every file-level check.\0A\0AAND THE REPLACE IS A SILENT NO-OP OUTSIDE THE IDE'S OWN APPLICATION INSTANCE. Run from the addon's local instance it answers 'terminals retyped' with every error cluster zero and changes nothing. That is why this opens everything through Project\3AActive Project -> Application\2C and why A PROJECT MUST BE OPEN AND ACTIVE\3A with none open that hop answers Error 1055.\0A\0ATERMINALS ARE FOUND BY NAME\2C NEVER BY INDEX. Controls[] order is front-panel creation order for a generated VI and error-clusters-first for a template-built one\2C so an index is not portable. The Case Structure is there because Search 1D Array answers -1 for a miss and Index Array then CLAMPS TO ELEMENT 0 - which would silently retype the error cluster instead. 'terminals retyped' is the check\3A it must equal the number of names asked for.\0A\0AEVERY REFNUM IS CLOSED. Leaking the refnum a class open returns keeps the class in LabVIEW's memory past a project close\2C so the next run binds to a stale copy.\0A\0APER-STAGE ERROR INDICATORS ARE DELIBERATE\3A a merged error chain names only the invoke node\2C and this diagram has many.">
